"fact": "Taliglucerase alfa (Elelyso) is a human enzyme made by genetically engineered carrot cells grown in bioreactors, according to its FDA label. The plant cells give the enzyme mannose-tipped sugar chains that help macrophages take it up. The FDA approved it in 2012 for Type 1 Gaucher disease, and it is widely cited as the first FDA-approved protein drug made in plant cells.",
