"fact": "The three FDA-approved hyaluronidase products come from different sources: Amphadase is purified from bovine (cow) testicles, Vitrase from ovine (sheep) testicles, and Hylenex recombinant is human hyaluronidase made in genetically engineered Chinese Hamster Ovary cells. Vitrase was approved in 2004 and Hylenex in 2005, and all three are labeled to help injected fluids and drugs spread through tissue by breaking down hyaluronan.",
