"hook": "A surgical clotting protein made with help from snake venom 🐍",
"fact": "Recothrom, a recombinant topical thrombin approved by the FDA in 2008, is made in Chinese Hamster Ovary cells, and a snake-derived protein is used in the manufacturing step that activates it, so its label lists hamster and snake protein hypersensitivity concerns. Like the bovine and human-plasma thrombins, it is applied only to oozing tissue surfaces and is never injected.",
