"fact": "Kebilidi (eladocagene exuparvovec-tneq), approved by the FDA in November 2024, is the first FDA-approved gene therapy for AADC deficiency, a rare disorder in which the brain cannot make enough dopamine. A harmless virus shell carries a working DDC gene, and it is infused in four tiny 0.08 mL doses directly into the putamen during a single stereotactic brain surgery.",
